Titre$ H E L V E L L A   -   DISSING (1966)
Com$ The Genus Helvella in Europe DANSK BOTANISK ARKIV, Bind25, Nr.l  -  Adapté par Paul Bertéa 24-11-2013

1,2 $ Fruitbody subsessile
1,5 $ Stipe distinct, sulcate, with deep longitudinal furrows
1,15 $ Stipe distinct, even, terete, occasionally with a few, indistinct grooves near the base

2,3 $ Hymenium black
2,4 $ Hymenium pale greyish-brown or dark brownish, outside with a few grooves below, or with whitish, sharp-edged ribs

3,0 $ Apothecium 0.5-2 cm broad, cup flat, 0.5-1 cm high, hymenium and upperpart of outside black. Outside at least near the margin pubescent; stipe indistinct, with a few grooves. Spores ellipsoid, 21-23.7-25x11-12.8-14 µm. December to March, Algeria, Portugal, and France (cfr.H.corium) p.45 $ H. helvellula 
3,0 $ Apothecium 2-10 cm broad, cup deep,1-5 cm high, with crenate margin, when adult often expanded and split into irregular lobes, hymenium black, upperpart of outside whitish to dark greyish-brown. Outside pubescent; stipe low, but mostly broad, witb a few grooves, solid or inside with cavities. Spores oval, 20-21.9-24x11-12.1-13 µm. December to June, allover Europe, on calcareous soil. p.36 $ H. leucomelaena

4,0 $ Apothecium 2-10 cm broad, cup deep,1-5 cm high, with crenate margin, when adult often expanded, split into irregular lobes, hymenium pale greyish-brown to dark brownish, upperpart of outside whitish to dark greyish-brown (see3:2) p.36 $ H. leucomelaena
4,0 $ Apothecium 1-3 cm broad, 0.5-1.5 cm high,cup-shaped, hymenium dark brownish, outside concolorous above or whitish near the margin; stipe low, with whitish, sharp-edged ribs, continuing on outside. Outside pubescent, especially near the margin. Spores 16-17.7-19x11-11.8-12 µm. June-September, in Dryas vegetation in arctic-alpine areas, Greenland, Svalbard, Norway, Sweden, Switzerland. A form of H. acetabulum (see also 14:2) p.49 $ H. acetabulum

5,6 $ Outside of pileus naked
5,9 $ Outside of pileus (cup) pubescent, or villose near the margin

6,0 $ Hymenium whitish to cream, the whole outside of fruitbody whitish. Pileus 1.5-3 cm broad, connivent saddle-shaped, regular or irregularly lobed, adnate, outside naked, wavy; stipe 2-3 cm high, 8-12 mm broad, with deep longitudinal furrows, ribs sharp-edged, anastomozing; on drying the hymenium becomes reddish-brown, the stipe bright yellowish. Spores 15.5-16.8-18x10-10.8-12 µm. p.108 $ H. lactea
6,7 $ Hymenium greyish to greyish-brown to brown to black

7,0 $ Pileus 0.5-1.5 cm broad, convex, hemispheric, or rarely tending to be compressed, margin free. Hymenium dark brownish to black, outside whitish, naked; stipe with prominent, rarely anastomozing, sharp-edged ribs, continuing on outside of pileus. Spores small, 15-15.5-16x9-9.5-10 µm. France, Switzerland p.110 $ H. phlebophora 
7,0 $ Pileus saucer-shaped to discoid, rarely recurving, margin entirely free. Hymenium black, outside grey to black; stipe with 4-6 irregular, longitudinal furrows, ribs blunt, rarely anastomozing, continuing on outside of pileus, but never reaching the margin. Iceland and, Sweden, in deep moss p.112 $ H. philonotis 
7,8 $ Pileus regularly saddle-shaped to irregularly lobed, adnate

8,0 $ Hymenium pale brownish, outside naked or delicately pubescent, whitish, with manylow, but distinct, branching, anastomozing ribs, continuing from the pale brownish stipe. Pileus 1.5-4 cm broad, saddle-shaped or with irregular lobes, outside whitish; stipe 2-6 cm high, 8-20 mm broad, with deep longitudinal furrows, ribs sharp-edged, anastomozing. Spores 17-18.4-21x11-12-13 µm.April-June, Holland and South Europe, attached to Populus p.92 $ H. fusca 
8,0 $ Hymenium grey to greyish-brown to black, outside naked, greyish; stipe greyish to greyish-brown, in arctic-alpine areas often almost black. Pileus 1.5-5 cm broad, regularly saddle-shaped, or with 2-4 regular lobes, or irregularly lobed, adnate, hymenium often wrinkled-folded towards the center; outside sometimes with indistinct low ribs,continuing from the stipe, which is 1.5-10 cm high, 5-15 mm broad, with irregular, longitudinal, deep furrows, ribs normally anastomozing, with sharp edges, sometimes even double-edged. Spores 15-17.1-19x9.5-11.2-12 µm. Pileus convex, hemispheric, hymenium dark brownish; stipe with conspicuous, regular, blunt, rarely anastomozing ribs, continuing on outside of pileus. Pileus 2-3 cm broad; stipe2-3.5 cm high, 8-12 mm broad, whole outside whitish, pubescent. Spores 17-17.6-19x11-12-13.5 µm. Denmark and South Europe p.95 $ H. queletiana 

9,10 $ Pileus deflexed, regularly saddle-shaped or with irregular lobes, hymenium whitish or pale brownish; stipe with deep, irregular, longitudinal furrows,ribs sharp-edged, anastomozing
9,11 $ Apothecium cup-shaped

10,0 $ Hymenium whitish to cream,outside pubescent, pale brownish, stipe whitish. Pileus 1.5-6 cm broad, hymenium on dried specimens cream, margin first inrolled, when adult expanded, adnate; stipe prominent, 3-8 cm high, 5-25 mm broad. August-November. p.85 $ H. crispa 
10,0 $ Hymenium pale brownish, outside naked or delicately pubescent, whitish, with many low, but distinct, branching, anastomozing ribs, continuing from the pale brownish stipe. Pileus 1.5-4 cm broad, saddle-shaped or with 2-4 lobes, adnate, hymenium on drying dark brownish; stipe 2-6 cm high, 8-20 mm broad. April-June, Holland and South Europe, attached to Populus. p.92 $ H. fusca

11,12 $ Stipe with blunt ribs, not continuing on outside of apothecium
11,13 $ Stipe gradually widening into apothecium, with sharp-edged or blunt ribs, continuing on outside of apothecium

12,0 $ Small, first compressed, then regular, hemispheric, cup 1-3 cm broad, stipe 1-2.5 cm high. Spores 19-21.7-24x12-13.1-15 µm. Cup deep, hymenium greyish to greyish-brown, outside pubescent, concolorous with hymenium or gradually becoming whitish towards the stipe; stipe distinct, with 2-5 blunt ribs. February-June, on calcareous soil, often gregarious p.41 $ H. solitaria 
12,0 $ Medium to large, cup regular, saucer-shaped, when adult margin sometimes recurved and irregular, 2-8 cm broad; stipe 2-6 cm high. Spores 17-19.1-21x11-12.3-13.5 µm. Cup low, hymenium pale brownish to dark greyish-brown, outside pubescent, pale yellowish-grey to greyish-brown; stipe distinct, with 4-7 regular, blunt ribs, occasionally compressed, whitish to cream to pale greyish. April-October (in arctic-alpine areas the stipe is sometimes very short) p.73 $ H. queletii 

13,0 $ Hymenium greyish to pale greyish-brown; stipe with prominent, blunt, branching, greyish-white ribs. Spores 15-17.6-19x10-11.5-13 µm. June-September. Apothecium 1.5-7 cm broad, outside pubescent, concolorous with hymenium above, below paler, greyish to whitish p.56 $ H. costifera 
13,14 $ Hymenium pale brownish to dark brown, sometimes with a violet tinge. March-June.

14,0 $ Stipe low, with prominent, branching, blunt, pale brownish ribs. Spores 17-19.2-21x13-14.6-16 µm. Apothecium 1-3.5 cm broad, hymenium dark brownish, outside pubescent, concolorous with hymenium above, below gradually paler. March-May, Central and South Europe p.60 $ H. unicolor 
14,0 $ Stipe 2-6 cm high, with branching, angular to sharp-edged, whitish to cream ribs. Spores 16-17.7-19x11-11.8-12 µm. Apothecium 1.5-7 cm broad, hymenium pale brownish to dark brown, sometimes with a violet tinge, outside pubescent, dark greyish-brown above, below paler, whitish to cream.April-June (see also 4:2) p.49 $ H. acetabulum 

15,16 $ Outside naked, pileus saddle-shaped, deflexed or convex
15,20 $ Outside pubescent to villose, pileus saddle-shaped or cup-shaped

16,17 $ Hymenium dark brownish to black
16,19 $ Hymenium whitish or pale brownish, often with a violet tinge

17,0 $ Stipe pubescent to villose, greyish to greyish-brown, outside of pileus naked, grey to dark greyish. Pileus 1-2 cm broad, saddle-shaped or irregularly expanded, on adult specimens adnate, hymenium black; stipe 2-4 cm high, 2-4 mm broad, terete or compressed, solid, occasionally with indistinct grooves near the whitish base p.121 $ H. atra 
17,18 $ Stipe and outside of pileus naked, whitish

18,0 $ Pileus 1-3.5 cm broad; stipe prominent, hollow, 2-6 cm high, 5-15 mm broad. Spores large, 21-21.9-24x13-14.4-15 µm. Saddle-shaped or with three lobes, hymenium dark brownish to black, outside whitish to very pale greyish-white. February-June, Germany, Holland, France, South Europe, on sandy soil p.138 $ H. leucopus
18,0 $ Pileus 0.5-1.5 cm broad; stipe solid or hollow, 2-4 cm high, 2-5 mm broad. Spores medium, 19-20.5-22x11-12.1-14 µm. Saddle-shaped or with three lobes, hymenium dark brownish to black, outside whitish to cream, on drying pale brownish. July-October, on calcareous soil p.136 $ H. albella 

19,0 $ Deflexed, saddle-shaped, margin entirely free, hymenium whitish to cream. Spores broad, 18-19.4-21x13.5-14.8-18 µm. Pileus 1.5-3 cm broad, outside and stipe whitish; stipe 4-7 cm high, 3-7 mm broad p.135 $ H. latispora 
19,0 $ Convex, campanulate to saddle-shaped, margin adnate, hymenium pale brownish, sometimes with a violet tinge. Spores medium, 18-19.2-21x11-12-13.5 µm. Pileus 1-3.5 cm broad, outside and stipe whitish to cream; stipe 1.5-5(-10) cm high,3-7(-10) mm broad p.128 $ H. elastica 

20,21 $ Involute to saddle-shaped
20,24 $ Cup-shaped

21,22 $ Hymenium dark brownish to black
21,23 $ Hymenium whitish to pale brownish, or greyish

22,0 $ Outside of pileus naked, grey to dark greyish, hymenium black; stipe pubescent to villose, grey to greyish-brown. Pileus 1-2 cm broad,saddle-shaped to irregularly expanded, on adult specimens adnate; stipe 2-4 cm high, 2-4 mm broad, terete, solid, occasionally within distinct grooves near the base p.121 $ H. atra 
22,0 $ Outside of pileus villose, greyish-brown to dark brownish, hymenium dark brownish to black; stipe villose, concolorous with outside of pileus. Pileus 0.8-2.5 cm broad, involute to saddle-shaped, margin normally free; stipe 1.5-6 cm high, 3-5 mm broad, terete, solid, occasionally within-distinct grooves near the yellowish-white base p.117 $ H. pezizoides 

23,0 $ Hymenium grey to greyish-brown, pileus saddle-shaped to involute, with free margin, occasionally on adult specimens expanded, adnate. Pileus 0.5-1.5 cm broad, outside villose, pale greyish-brown to dark grey; stipe 1.5-3.5 cm high, 2-4 mm broad, villose, concolorous without side above, towards the base paler, greyish-white or greyish-yellow p.114 $ H. ephippium 
23,0 $ Hymenium whitish to cream, pileus involute to saddle-shaped, whole outside whitish, pubescent. Pileus 0.5-1.5 cm broad, margin permanently free; stipe 1.5-3(-5) cm high, 2-4 mm broad p.125 $ H. stevensii
23,0 $ Hymenium cream to pale brownish, pileus connivent saddle-shaped or irregularly lobed, outside concolorous with hymenium or slightly paler, delicately pubescent. Pileus 1-2.5 cm broad, occasionally adnate; stipe 2-4.5 cm high, 2-5 mm broad. Recognized only from D.S.A.(see Dissing & Lange 1967) $ H. connivens

24,0 $ Pileus regularly cup-shaped. Spores ellipsoid. Cup 2-3 cm broad, hymenium yellowish-brown to pale greyish-brown, outside villose, concolorous with hymenium or grey; stipe 2.5-4 cm high, 3-5 mm broad, villose, greyish p.62 $ H. macropus 
24,25 $ Pileus cup-shaped. Spores oval

25,0 $ Hymenium black, outside very dark brownish to black, though sometimes whitish near the margin. Cup 1-4 cm broad, first compressed, then regular, when adult often expanded, outside villose; stipe 0.5-2 cm high, 2-5 mm broad, solid, terete, with grooves near the sometimes yellowish-grey to whitish base, or compressed, with 2-3 inconspicuous blunt ribs. Spores 18-20-22x11-12.1-13 µm (cfr. H. helvellula, 3:1) p.79 $ H. corium 
25,0 $ Hymenium pale brownish to yellowish-brown, cup low, regular, 0.5-2 cm broad; stipe 0.8-1.5 cm high, 2-6 mm broad. Outside pubescent, greyish or yellowish-grey; stipe short, solid, terete, or slightly compressed with indistinct blunt ribs, pubescent, yellowish-white to cream p.71 $ H. cupuliformis 
25,0 $ Hymenium grey to steel grey to dark greyish-brown, cup1-2 cm broad, when adult often expanding, margin then split into several lobes; stipe 1-3 cm high, 2-4 mm broad. Gregarious. Outside pubescent to villose, dark greyish to dark brownish, stipe villose, terete, solid, concolorous with outside above, below gradually paler, near the base yellowish or whitish p.67 $ H. villosa 
